      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MRS MAHONEY (1) did a good job to come from a wider barrier and finish third last start, beaten 4.7 metres at Parkes. This is stronger but gets the inside draw and that should ensure a cosy run. SERGEANT PEE JAY (3) has been solid of late. Came from this barrier when fifth at his latest appearance at Cowra, beaten 7 metres. His lone win came at this circuit and distance and he should enjoy an economical run from this draw. JASPERSTIMETOSHINE (9) fell last start but draws for a trail and is a player off his second here three back. MOTHER WAS A MUDDA (4) drops in grade off the Canola Cup where he was runner-up in the heats.",
